      "title": "Exploiting System Management Mode with a very long interrupt",
      "url": "https://github.com/xoreaxeaxeax/smiiiiiiiiiiiiiiii",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49245491",
      "score": 178,
      "comments": 76,
      "author": "WhiteDawn",
      "published": "2026-08-10T16:03:14Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Delays in System Management Interrupt (SMI) handling create race conditions, allowing attackers to manipulate memory during x86 SMM state transitions.",
        "Successful exploitation bypasses Ring 0/hypervisor defenses, granting arbitrary code execution inside high-privilege SMRAM (Ring -2) firmware environments.",
        "Defense demands hardware-enforced SMRAM locking, vendor BIOS/UEFI updates, and proper Advanced Programmable Interrupt Controller (APIC) timing validations."
      ]
    },
